{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ClimaxVolumeMass.VertexAlgebraRelations","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ClimaxVolumeMass.VertexAlgebraRelations","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.HeckeGS","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.self_dual_curvature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.self_dual_curvature","kind":"axiom","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-relations.lean#L296-L304","doc":"C-7: The curvature [σᵢ, σⱼ] is self-adjoint under the antipode:\nS([σᵢ, σⱼ]) = [σᵢ, σⱼ] where [a, b] = ab(ba)⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.descartes_genus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.descartes_genus","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-relations.lean#L280-L282","doc":"C-4b: χ = 2 - 2g = -6 forces g = 4. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:vertex-algebra-relations","label":"prop:vertex-algebra-relations","md":"quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-relations.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.dq_squared_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.dq_squared_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-relations.lean#L265-L274","doc":"C-2: The obstruction coefficient q⁻¹(1-q⁻¹) is nonzero for q > 1.\nThis proves d_q² ≠ 0 on vertical forms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.trace_ne_trace_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.trace_ne_trace_inv","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-relations.lean#L249-L257","doc":"**The negation of the withdrawn QUO-3a.** Over a domain, if `h ≠ 0` and\n`τ(1) ≠ 0` then `τ(x) ≠ τ(x⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.sum_trace_sub_trace_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.sum_trace_sub_trace_inv","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-relations.lean#L240-L247","doc":"Summed over `k` generators: `Σᵢ τ(xᵢ − xᵢ⁻¹) = k·h·τ(1)`. With `k = n − 1`\nthis is the corrected left-hand side of the withdrawn QUO-3a. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.trace_sub_trace_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.trace_sub_trace_inv","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-relations.lean#L231-L238","doc":"**Skein balance of a linear trace.** For a Hecke generator `x`\n(`x² = h·x + 1`) with left inverse `y`, every `R`-linear functional `τ`\nsatisfies `τ(x) − τ(x⁻¹) = h·τ(1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.hecke_inv_eq_sub_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.hecke_inv_eq_sub_smul","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-relations.lean#L223-L229","doc":"A left inverse of a Hecke generator is `x − h·1` (so it is the inverse). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.observability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.observability","kind":"axiom","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-relations.lean#L195-L202","doc":"QUO-2: An element commuting with all generators under conjugation\nis a scalar. Equivalent to Hom(1, Ad(A)) = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.markov_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.markov_nondegenerate","kind":"axiom","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-relations.lean#L178-L189","doc":"QU-3c: Non-degeneracy —\nthe Markov trace pairing (f, g) ↦ tr_M(f · g) is non-degenerate\non GS normal forms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.markov_stabilisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.markov_stabilisation","kind":"axiom","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-relations.lean#L166-L176","doc":"QU-3b: Markov stabilisation —\ntr_M(f · σ_n) = δ⁻¹ · tr_M(f) where δ = -(q + q⁻¹). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.markov_conjugation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.markov_conjugation","kind":"axiom","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-relations.lean#L155-L164","doc":"QU-3a: Markov conjugation invariance —\ntr_M(σᵢ · f) = tr_M(f · σᵢ) for all i and f. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.AlgElement.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.AlgElement.mul","kind":"axiom","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-relations.lean#L120-L126","doc":"**AlgElement.mul** — convolution on monomials.  Axiomatised\npending concrete formal-algebra ring structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.AlgElement.embed_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.AlgElement.embed_succ","kind":"axiom","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-relations.lean#L110-L118","doc":"**AlgElement.embed_succ** — embed H_n into H_{n+1} by treating\ngenerators as σ₀,…,σ_{n-1}.  Axiomatised pending the concrete\nHecke-algebra implementation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAlgebra.MarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAlgebra.MarkovTrace","kind":"axiom","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/vertex-algebra-relations.lean#L94-L108","doc":"The Markov trace tr_M : AlgElement(HeckeGen n, ℝ) → ℝ.\nDefined by the two Markov properties on normal forms.\n\nThis extends the Gröbner–Shirshov framework with a linear functional\nsatisfying conjugation invariance and stabilisation. The existence\nand uniqueness is Jones 1987, Theorem 5.1.\n\n**Markov trace** on H_n(q) — axiomatised pending the full\nMarkov-recursion-on-GS-normal-forms implementation in the\ntransfer-matrix framework. ","signatureChunk":0}]}